# Toast

A corner notification answering one question: did my action work?
Rendered from the Rails flash. Each toast carries a dismiss button;
success, info and warning toasts also auto-dismiss after 3 s, while
error toasts stay until the reader closes them.

<%= embed :toast, :variants %>

## When to use

- Reporting the outcome of the user's own action after a redirect:
  saved, added, removed, merge failed.
- Set the flash in the controller; the layout's `toast` partial does
  the rest.

## When not to use

- Ongoing page or data state — `alert`, which persists (see the
  *Feedback* pattern page: a toast can expire unseen).
- Anything the user must not miss — critical clinical information is
  never a toast.
- Asking a question — toasts carry no actions; a decision is a
  `dialog`.

## Usage

`render_toast` (`Gesso::Components::ToastHelper`) maps each flash entry to a
toast category, role and icon, then renders the toaster — one toast per
entry, nothing when the flash is empty. Set the flash in the controller;
render it once in the layout.

```erb
<%%= render_toast(flash: flash) %>
```

## Flash types

The flash type drives the category, colour, icon and dismiss behaviour.
Use `notice` for success and `alert` for failure in controllers — the
mapping does the categorising. Unknown types fall back to `info`.

| Flash type | Category | When to use | Dismisses |
| ---------- | -------- | ----------- | --------- |
| `notice` | success | Confirm an action succeeded. | after 3 s |
| `info` | info | Neutral, incidental information. | after 3 s |
| `warning` | warning | Caution about the outcome. | after 3 s |
| `alert` / `error` | error | An action failed. | on dismiss only |

## Dismissing

Every toast has a dismiss button (the vendored `toast.js` closes a toast
on a click inside its `<footer>`). By default **error toasts do not
auto-dismiss** — a failed clinical action should not vanish unseen — so
the button is their only way to close. The per-category colour
(`toast.css`) keys off the clinical tokens, mirroring the alert variants.

`auto_dismiss` overrides the default for the whole render:

| `auto_dismiss` | Behaviour |
| -------------- | --------- |
| omitted (default) | Errors persist; everything else auto-dismisses (3 s). |
| `true` | Everything auto-dismisses (errors 5 s, else 3 s). |
| `false` | Everything persists until dismissed. |

```erb
<%%= render_toast(flash: flash, auto_dismiss: true) %>
```

## Do and don't

- Do write the outcome, past tense, naming the object: "Referral
  saved", "Patient records merged" (see *Content*).
- Do use `notice` for success and `alert` for failure in
  controllers — the mapping does the categorising.
- Don't queue several toasts for one action; one action, one
  outcome.
- Don't restate the obvious page change ("Page loaded") — toast
  only what the user can't already see.

## Accessibility and content

- One line, no period needed, no actions besides dismiss — anything
  needing a response belongs in the page or a dialog.
- The dismiss button is icon-only; its `aria-label` ("Dismiss") gives
  it an accessible name.
- Even though error toasts persist until dismissed, pair an error toast
  with the page showing the failure state — never make the toast the
  only record of it.
